# Line endings.
#
# Without this, Git uses each machine's core.autocrlf, so a Windows checkout
# commits CRLF and a Linux one commits LF, and every file shows as modified
# depending on who touched it last. Declaring it once removes that whole class of
# noise: files are stored with LF and checked out however the platform prefers.
* text=auto

# Binary assets. Git must never try to normalise these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.exe binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Keep the lockfile diffable but out of merge conflicts nobody can resolve by hand.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
